# Boroko POS Legacy - Configuration
#
# DEPLOYMENT MODEL: Local config file (preferred)
# On first run, the POS terminal prompts for Supabase URL and anon key.
# Values are stored in <userData>/pos-config.json (Windows: %APPDATA%/Boroko POS Legacy/).
# No environment variables are required for normal operation.
#
# ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE FALLBACK (optional):
# If pos-config.json does not exist, the app falls back to these env vars.
# Useful for automated deployments where you pre-bake values at build time.
# The anon key is Supabase's public-facing key (not a secret).

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_KEY=<anon-public-key>
